$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 BLUCOMSIG {
  coords 69.676 99.781 76.216
  m_sTitle "Command & signals"
  m_sTextData "<h2>CALLSIGNS</h2>"\
  "HQ - 11"\
  "OC - 11A"\
  "SGT - 11B"\
  "1SEC  - 11C"\
  "2SEC - 11D"\
  "3SEC - 11E"\
  ""\
  "<h2>FREQ/CHAN</h2>"\
  "All callsigns - 48mhz"\
  ""\
  "<h2>PYROTECHNICS</h2>"\
  "White smoke/flare - Maneuvers/Illuimnation"\
  "Green smoke/flare - Friendly location"\
  "Red smoke/flare - Enemy location"\
  ""\
  "<h2>PASSWORDS</h2> "\
  "All passwords can be changed at CO's discretion. "\
  "• <b>Challenge:<b> Birthday | <b>Password:</b> Boy "\
  "• Running password: 21 "
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 6
 }
 BLUEN {
  coords 97.468 98.308 67.825
  m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "Enemy forces consist of Argentine Army elements operating within the area of operations."\
  "Current enemy strength and composition is unknown. However, we should assume the enemy force is larger than our own and plan accordingly."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
  "• Enemy forces have identified our location and are expected to maintain contact throughout our withdrawal."\
  "• With no other British forces currently operating within the area of operations, Argentine forces are free to manoeuvre without opposition and may establish blocking positions or cut-off points along our withdrawal route."\
  ""\
  "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
  "• Unknown."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 4
 }
 BLUFRIEND {
  coords 114.74 101.531 35.051
  m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "We are 1 Platoon, A Company, 1st Battalion, Welsh Guards."\
  "Our force consists of 27 personnel currently assembled at the harbour area, GRID: 006002"\
  ""\
  "Our harbour area is arranged in a triangular formation, with shell scrape positions established at each point and along the perimeter. Platoon HQ occupies its own shell scrape in the centre of the formation."\
  "These are shallow dug positions offering only limited protection and should not be considered suitable for prolonged defence."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
  "• None."\
  ""\
  "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
  "• Land Rovers at the extraction area carry additional ammunition and supplies, allowing the platoon to resupply while awaiting stragglers before extraction."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 3
 }
 BLUMIS {
  coords 107.813 121.571 163.85
  m_sTitle "Mission"
  m_sTextData "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
  "We are to conduct a <b>FIGHTING WITHDRAWAL</b> to our extraction area in the north-east in order to rally with our vehicles and leave the AO."\
  ""\
  "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
  "Our platoon harbour has been compromised following a deliberate Argentine assault. The enemy's objective is to overrun the harbour, destroy the platoon, and prevent our withdrawal."\
  ""\
  "Remaining within the harbour will only allow the enemy to build momentum and surround our position. Instead, we are to break out of the harbour, fight through enemy blocking positions, and withdraw to our waiting Land Rovers at the designated extraction point."\
  ""\
  "Maintain unit cohesion, avoid becoming decisively engaged, and ensure as much of the platoon as possible reaches the extraction area. Once enough surviving personnel have reached the rally we'll withdraw."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 BLUSIT {
  coords 96.137 98.971 70.664
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
  "DTL: 18/04/1982, 0602hrs, Longmoor Training Area, South of England."\
  ""\
  "Weather: Overcast with heavy rain, light winds, visibility 1km-, with no significant forecast of change."\
  ""\
  "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
  "The Falklands War is underway. As British forces prepare for deployment to the South Atlantic, units across the United Kingdom are conducting intensive pre-deployment training to ensure they are ready for operations against Argentine forces."\
  ""\
  "1 Platoon, A Company, 1st Battalion, Welsh Guards, is currently taking part in a field exercise at Longmoor Training Area. The platoon has established a temporary harbour area while rehearsing tactical movement, harbour drills, and withdrawal procedures ahead of deployment."\
  ""\
  "During the early hours of the morning, Argentine reconnaissance elements unexpectedly located the harbour and launched a deliberate assault in an attempt to overrun the position before the platoon could react. With the harbour compromised, the platoon has been ordered to break contact, fight its way back to the extraction point, and withdraw from the area before being cut off."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 1
 }
}